course: dictionary
lesson: 2576
title: Democracy: rule by the people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A democracy is a country where the people choose their leaders by voting. The word comes from old Greek words meaning rule by the people. Look at the clues in the sentence to check your understanding: «They called it democracy, rule by the people, though women, slaves and foreigners could not vote.»
explain: The sentence shows that democracy is about who has the power, and it also shows that a country can say it is a democracy when not everyone is included. Words like «free» and «elections» are clues too. If a country has free elections and free speech, people can say what they think and vote for who they want.
explain: You can also meet democracy in small ways. Your class might vote for a class leader. Everyone has an equal say, which is one meaning of democracy. Try putting your meaning into a sentence: «Our class is a small democracy» makes sense if you think of people voting.
fact: Democracy means a way of running a country where the people choose their leaders by voting.
fact: «A democracy» means a country run in this way.
fact: «Live in a democracy» means living in a country where people can vote for their leaders.
fact: In a class vote, everyone has an equal say, which is a small kind of democracy.
fact: «Germany was a democracy after 1919, but Hitler's party took power in 1933 and ended it.» This shows that a democracy can lose its freedoms.
exercise: «Democracy is a way of running a country in which the people choose their leaders by voting.» What does democracy mean? | A country ruled by one king | *A way of running a country where people choose leaders by voting | A type of sausage sold at a school fair | A place where people sell things
exercise: «They called it democracy, rule by the people, though women, slaves and foreigners could not vote.» What does «rule by the people» tell us? | Only the king has the power | *The people have the power to choose their leaders | People must pay money to vote | Everyone is a slave
exercise: Our class votes for a class leader. What is this like? | *A small democracy | A zoo | A kingdom ruled by one person | A dictatorship
test: «Germany was a democracy after 1919, but Hitler's party took power in 1933 and ended it.» What does this show? | Democracy always lasts forever | Hitler started democracy | Germany had no leaders | *Democracy can be lost
test: «Live in a democracy» means what? | Live in a house with a door | Live in a tent | *Live in a country where people vote for their leaders | Live under a king
exam: Which of these is a sign of a democracy? | *Free elections where people vote | Laws made by a single person | A ruler who never asks anyone | Leaders chosen by one family
